end that amount each year, if over zero, from the General Fund to the Public School Employees’ Retirement System account. The money would be used to help cover the system’s unfunded liabilities, and the act would take effect in 60 days.","aiSummaryBasis":"bill text","aiSummaryModel":"gpt-5.4-mini","aiSummaryGenerated":"2026-11-05","aiSummaryThin":false},"PA-2025-HB2867":{"id":"PA-2025-HB2867","passed":false,"number":"HB 2867","title":"An Act providing for supplemental payments to households eligible for the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Program and for emergency utility payments; imposing duties on the Department of Human Services; and making an interfund transfer.","summary":null,"summarySource":null,"introduced":"2026-10-28","sponsor":{"name":"Doyle Heffley","party":"R","state":"PA","district":"122"},"cosponsors":[{"name":"R. Lee James","party":"R","state":"PA","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Brenda Pugh","party":"R","state":"PA","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Tina Pickett","party":"R","state":"PA","date":null,"withdrawn":false},{"name":"Pat Gallagher","party":"D","state":"PA","date":null,"withdrawn":false}],"cosponsorCount":4,"committees":[],"actions":[{"date":"2026-10-28","text":"Referred to Consumer Protection, Technology & Utilities","chamber":"House"}],"law":null,"policyArea":null,"url":"https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/2025/hb2867","textUrl":"https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/text/HTM/2025/0/HB2867/PN4105","versions":[{"label":"Printer's No. PN4105","date":null,"url":"https://www.palegis.us/legislation/bills/text/HTM/2025/0/HB2867/PN4105","type":"HTML"}],"votes":[],"documents":[],"dataAsOf":"2026-11-01","aiSummary":"The bill would give extra LIHEAP payments to households that qualify for the Low-Income Home Energy Assistance Program, based on their expected cash and crisis benefits for the 2026-2027 season. It would also give a one-time $200 emergency utility payment to households with income at or below 250% of the federa